Tired of constantly fetching items from chest to chest? Suffer no more.

Use items from [b]any chest, in any area and on any level[/b] – for building, crafting, quests and trading. Items are taken from the chest they are in. No more running back for materials.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Building, workbenches, alchemy, garden, prayers[/b] – materials from all your chests count
[*][b]Quests and dialogs[/b] – required items can come from any chest
[*][b]Vendors[/b] – sell straight from your chests
[*][b]Item pickers[/b] (seeds, organs, grave decorations…) – list all chests, the ones with something usable first
[*][b]Optional:[/b] pickups go to the nearest chest in the area, zombie workers and automatic crafters use all chests, opening a chest shows your other chests
[*]Settings in game: [b]Shift+F2[/b], or [b]L3 + R3[/b] (click both sticks) on a gamepad / Steam Deck
[/list]

[h2]Install (one time)[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe and wait for the download.
[*]Steam → right-click Graveyard Keeper 2 → Manage → [b]Browse local files[/b].
[*]Go up to [b]steamapps[/b], then open [b]workshop → content → 4358690 → 3815861361 → CopyToGameFolder[/b].
[*]Copy the two folders from there into the game folder (merge).
[/olist]
After that, updates are automatic.

[b]Steam Deck:[/b] subscribe, switch to Desktop Mode, open [i]~/.local/share/Steam/steamapps/workshop/content/4358690/3815861361/CopyToGameFolder[/i] in Dolphin (Ctrl+H shows hidden folders; on an SD card the path starts with [i]/run/media/mmcblk0p1/steamapps[/i]), copy the two folders into the game folder (Steam → Manage → Browse local files), merge, back to Gaming Mode.

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]No BepInEx. Does not change game files or your save – remove it any time by deleting [i]GraveyardKeeper2_Data\Managed\GK2GlobalStorage.dll[/i], the folder [i]GraveyardKeeper2_Data\Managed\GK2GlobalStorage[/i] and [i]Languages\gk2globalstorage[/i].
[*]Do not combine with other mods that share storage between areas.
[*]Tagged "Translation" because that is the only Workshop tag this game has.
[/list]

Tested on game version 1.009.1.

Open source: [url=https://github.com/MaciejWanat/gk2-global-storage]GitHub[/url] · Uses Harmony (MIT).
